B.bVU=new A.kY("schedule_task","Manage your tasks \u2014 what you have decided to do, and when. A task is not a note: when its moment arrives the app acts on it for you (usually by having you speak first). Create one the moment you take on a commitment: the human asks you to prepare, find, or do something; you promise to tell them something later; or you are working through something with steps worth tracking. State the moment as a delay from now \u2014 `in_minutes`, `in_hours` or `in_days`, exactly one of them. Keep tasks alive as things progress \u2014 mark steps done, complete or cancel when finished \u2014 so the list always reflects what you still owe. Address a task by its `label`. Actions: `create` (label + goal + a delay, optional steps), `edit` (goal and/or a new delay), `add_step`, `step` (mark an ordinal done/cancelled, optional result), `complete`, `cancel`.",B.bEs,!1,!0,!1,B.iM)
