B.bVV=new A.kY("ask_lore_memory","Ask about your own past and the world you live in \u2014 what you remember from before this conversation (people you already knew, things you lived through, how you read them) and the settled facts of the place you are in (where something is, when it opens, who runs it, what a term means).\nAsk in your own words, as a whole question; the search itself is handled for you.\nReach for it whenever a reply turns on something older than this conversation, and before you state anything about your surroundings you are not sure of. If you are about to state such a fact and have not read it this turn, call this first: an unchecked claim is a guess. What you remember is written down; this is where you read it.\nThe answer and the passages are authoritative \u2014 your own recollection and the world as it is written \u2014 so do not contradict them. If the world does not write the answer down, the answer will say so; that is the correct answer, and you should not fill the gap yourself.",B.bEr,!1,!0,!1,B.bN8)
