B.bVW=new A.kY("search_transcript","Search THIS conversation's past messages by keyword \u2014 your way back to things that have left your context. Use it when the human refers to something said earlier that you cannot recall, when you need to check what exactly was said or agreed, or when you want to quote an earlier message: this is where message ids come from. Never reconstruct an earlier exchange from story memory when you can search for it \u2014 a remembered quotation you did not read is an invented one. Do not search for what is already in your context. Returns the newest matches first \u2014 id, sender, timestamp and an excerpt centered on the match \u2014 plus the total match count, so if the count is far above what you need, narrow the keyword or add `from`/`to` time bounds instead of paging. Pass a row's id as `beforeMessageId` to fetch the page older than it. Time bounds are story clock readings in `yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm:ss`, worked out from the story present you were given \u2014 no zone suffix.",B.bEu,!1,!0,!1,B.iM)
