B.bVX=new A.kY("browse_lore_memory","Browse your own past and the world you live in directly, without searching them. Three resolutions, decided by the arguments, each paged:\n- **No arguments** \u2014 the shelf: every lore base you can read, with what each is for.\n- **`loreBase`** \u2014 that lore base's entries, by title and length (no prose).\n- **`loreBase` and `entry`** \u2014 that entry's chunks, in order. Add `query` to keep only chunks whose text contains it (SQLite LIKE, case-insensitive for ASCII); omit it to read the entry whole, a chunk-page at a time.\nEvery result starts with \"Page X of Y \xb7 N items\", so page on while X < Y. Prefer `ask_lore_memory` when you have a question; prefer this when you want the material itself. Before you state a fact from your past or the world, read it here or with `ask_lore_memory` \u2014 what you have not read this turn is not yours to assert. What it returns is your own recollection and the world's settled facts, and it is authoritative.",B.bGY,!1,!0,!1,B.iM)
