B.bW_=new A.kY("browse_stickers",'List the stickers you may send, as ready-to-write lines:\n- **No arguments** \u2014 every sticker you can send, your own pack first: the stickers made for you, often drawn from your own face.\n- **`pack`** \u2014 only the stickers of one pack you can send from, named as the app names it.\n- **`query`** \u2014 only stickers whose meaning contains a word (case-insensitive); use it to find the right reaction.\nEach line is `[sticker] <handle> \u2014 <meaning>`. When a reply carries a feeling, browse here and send one: a picture shows what words flatten, and a character who never shows a face reads like a narrator. To send that sticker, write its line in your final answer, on a line of its own and without the leading dash: the app renders the picture, and the reader never sees the tag. Prefer your own pack \u2014 its stickers are yours alone \u2014 and fall back to a shared pack only when none of yours fits.\nThe handles here are the only valid ones: never invent a handle, and never take one from the transcript \u2014 an older turn may name a sticker you can no longer send. Copy the handle exactly; a shortened or altered one sends nothing.\nEvery result starts with "Page X of Y \xb7 N stickers you can send", so page on while X < Y.',B.bGZ,!1,!0,!1,B.iM)
